<title>UK: UK to cut tax relief on profit-related pay - FT.</title>
<headline>UK to cut tax relief on profit-related pay - FT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The British Treasury has decided it must cut tax relief on profit-related pay in the next 12 months, the Financial Times said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The move could hit the take-home pay of more than 2.5 million people in Britain.</p>
<p>The newspaper said government ministers were convinced they must stem the mounting costs of such schemes, which trebled to 1.5 billion stg last year.</p>
<p>They fear that if left unchecked, the Treasury could face a huge hole in revenues within five years, the Financial Times said. There was no immediate official comment on the report.</p>
